      "text": "To solve \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor\\), we need to determine the greatest integer that is less than or equal to \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\).\n\nFirst, calculate \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\):\n\\[\n-\\frac{5}{3} = -1.6667 \\ldots\n\\]\n\nTo find the floor value, we look for the largest integer that is less than or equal to \\(-1.6667\\). The integers around \\(-1.6667\\) are \\(-2\\) and \\(-1\\).\n\nSince \\(-1.6667 < -2\\), the floor value is \\(-2\\).\n\nThus, \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = -2\\).\n\nIn the form of an expression, this can be written as:\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = -2\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{-2}\\).",
